Hi,

Today, I've noticed that data completion does not work with object names containing "_" or ".". Here are a few examples:

a.b = list(a=1:3, b=4:6)
a.b$ #!wrongly says "object 'b' found"

a_b = list(a=1:3, b=4:6)
a_b$ #!wrongly says "object 'b' found"

ok <- list(not.ok=1, not_ok_either=2)
ok$not.ok$ #!names displayed are from the wrong level (same as if ok$...)
ok$not_ok_either$ #!names displayed are from the wrong level (same as if ok$...)

Could you check this out, e.g. improve the reg. expression patterns?
Thanks.

Marc

